: \"atletico-mg\",\n+    \"atletico paranaense\": \"atletico-pr\",\n+    \"ceara sporting club\": \"ceara\",\n+    \"parana\": \"parana\",\n+    \"america fc (minas gerais)\": \"america-mg\",\n+    \"america (minas gerais)\": \"america-mg\",\n+    \"sport club do recife\": \"sport\",\n+    \"vitoria ba\": \"vitoria\",\n+    \"gremio fbpa\": \"gremio\",\n+    \"clube de regatas do brasil\": \"flamengo\",  # defensive; not actually in data\n }\n \n \n _STATE_TOKENS = {\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-490c16ecf318/brazilian_soccer_mcp/team_normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-490c16ecf318/brazilian_soccer_mcp/team_normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-490c16ecf318/brazilian_soccer_mcp/team_normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-490c16ecf318/brazilian_soccer_mcp/team_normalize.py\n@@ -178,8 +178,19 @@\n     \"bolivar bol\": \"bolivar\",\n     # Suffix-stripped \"america - mg\" form seen in Brazilian_Cup_Matches\n     \"america - mg\": \"america-mg\",\n     \"america - rj\": \"america-rj\",\n+    # FIFA dataset full-name variants (accented in source, ASCII after strip)\n+    \"atletico mineiro\": \"atletico-mg\",\n+    \"atletico paranaense\": \"atletico-pr\",\n+    \"ceara sporting club\": \"ceara\",\n+    \"parana\": \"parana\",\n+    \"america fc (minas gerais)\": \"america-mg\",\n+    \"america (minas gerais)\": \"america-mg\",\n+    \"sport club do recife\": \"sport\",\n+    \"vitoria ba\": \"vitoria\",\n+    \"gremio fbpa\": \"gremio\",\n+    \"clube de regatas do brasil\": \"flamengo\",  # defensive; not actually in data\n }\n \n \n _STATE_TOKENS = {\n","additions":11,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/team_normalize.py","time":{"start":1788202162387,"end":1788202162389}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So FIFA data has \"Grêmio\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Fluminense\", etc. but NO \"Flamengo\" club name directly — Flamengo isn't in this FIFA dataset. The \"Flamengo\" query returns empty because there's no Flamengo club in FIFA data. That's actually correct behavior — Flamengo simply isn't in this FIFA dataset version.\n\nBut wait, my `top_rated_by_club` uses `club_key == key`. The club \"Grêmio\" normalizes to \"gremio\". A query for \"Grêmio\" should normalize to \"gremio\" and match. Let me verify the normalization handles the accented \"Grêmio\" — `_strip_accents(\"Grêmio\")` -> \"gremio\". Good.\n\nLet me test with Grêmio which exists.\n\nAlso issue: \"Atlético Mineiro\" normalizes — let me check. `_strip_accents` -> \"atletico mineiro\". Alias table has \"clube atletico mineiro\" -> \"atletico-mg\" and \"atletico mg\" -> \"atletico-mg\" but NOT \"atletico mineiro\". So \"atletico mineiro\" wouldn't match the alias and falls through to raw \"atletico mineiro\". Meanwhile query \"Atletico-MG\" -> \"atletico-mg\". Mismatch!\n\nI need to add aliases: \"atletico mineiro\" -> \"atletico-mg\". Similarly \"atletico paranaense\" -> alias exists as \"athletico paranaense\"? Let me check: alias table has \"athletico pr\" and \"athletico-paranaense\" and \"club athletico paranaense\". But FIFA uses \"Atlético Paranaense\" (with 'é'). Strip accents -> \"atletico paranaense\". Not in alias table. Need to add \"atletico paranaense\" -> \"atletico-pr\".\n\nAlso \"Sport Club do Recife\" -> strip -> \"sport club do recife\" -> alias \"sport club do recife\" -> \"sport\". Good.\n\n\"Ceará Sporting Club\" -> \"ceara sporting club\" not aliased -> falls through. Query \"Ceará\" -> \"ceara\" -> alias \"ceara\" -> \"ceara\". Mismatch.\n\nI need to improve the alias table / fallback. Better approach: make the fallback smarter — strip noise tokens (\"sc\", \"fc\", \"ec\", \"sporting\", \"club\", \"clube\", \"do\", \"da\", \"de\", \"recife\", \"mineiro\", \"paranaense\", \"paulista\", etc. — but careful, these city words are meaningful).\n\nActually a simpler robust approach: For the FIFA club matching, the issue is that \"Atlético Mineiro\" (FIFA) and \"Atletico-MG\" (match files) refer to the same club. The canonical should be the same. Let me add more aliases, and also add a secondary normalization that strips common descriptors.\n\nLet me enhance: add a fallback that strips common noise tokens and re-checks the alias table. Actually, let me add the specific missing aliases and add a \"descriptor-stripped\" fallback.\n\nAdd aliases:\n- \"atletico mineiro\" -> \"atletico-mg\"\n- \"atletico paranaense\" -> \"atletico-pr\"  \n- \"ceara sporting club\" -> \"ceara\"\n- \"ceara sc\" already -> \"ceara\"\n- \"parana\" -> \"parana\" (FIFA \"Paraná\")\n- \"america fc (minas gerais)\" -> \"america-mg\"\n- \"america (minas gerais)\" -> \"america-mg\"\n\nAnd a generic fallback: strip tokens like \"sc\", \"fc\", \"ec\", \"clube\", \"club\", \"sporting\", \"do\", \"da\", \"de\", \"esporte\", \"futebol\", \"paulista\", \"mineiro\", \"paranaense\", \"goianiense\", \"recife\", and parenthesized content, then re-lookup alias; if still no, use the stripped form.\n\nActually, let me add a robust second-pass: build canonical by removing parenthesized, removing noise tokens, collapsing, and if that reduced form matches an alias OR is shorter, use it. Let me implement a `_normalize_fifa_style` fallback.\n\nSimpler: extend the alias table with the FIFA variants. Let me do both — add the specific aliases AND add a noise-token stripping fallback pass.\n\nLet me also fix the competition filter to strip accents. I'll add a helper `_ascii_lower` for competition matching in queries.\n\nLet me update team_normalize.py to add aliases and a noise-stripping fallback, then update queries.py competition matching to strip accents.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0592798cb001lKFvJ3vjTEVzKI","sessionID":"ses_fa6dcf19cffe614Wrywmi9